* {{rhymes|en|ɒɡ|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|Q169994}}A [[noxious]] mixture of [[particulate]]s and [[gas]]es that is the result of [[urban]] [[air pollution]].
#: {{synonyms|en|pea-souper|pea-soup fog}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Martha Weinman Lear|title=Clare Boothe Luce, she who is behind ‘The Women’|magazine=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/1973/04/22/archives/on-harry-and-henry-and-ike-and-mr-shaw-clare-boothe-luce-she-who-is.html|date=22-04-1973|passage=A widow since 1967, she lives now in Honolulu because, she says, she can enjoy the Californialike climate without the '''smog'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2015|author=Richard Blackshire|title=Newtown Naughty Boy|page=145
|passage=Everyone smoked so if the auditorium was full, the whole room would be filled with smoke in next to no time. It was like the legendary London '''smog''' of the 1950s in there sometimes. You took it in turn to “flash the ash” as it was called.}}

