==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|transcenden}}, from {{der|en|fro|transcender}}, from {{der|en|la|transcendō||to climb over, step over, surpass, transcend}}, from {{m|la|trans||over}} + {{m|la|scandō||to climb}}; see [[scan]]; compare [[ascend]], [[descend]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/tɹæn(t)ˈsɛnd/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-transcend.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛnd|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[pass]] [[beyond]] the [[limit]]s of something.
#: {{ux|en|We cannot '''transcend''' what we refuse to face.}}
#* {{RQ:Bacon War with Spain|passage=such personal popes, emperors, or elective kings, as shall '''transcend''' their limits}}
#* {{quote-video game|en|developer=w:BioWare|title={{w|Mass Effect (video game)|Mass Effect}}|genre=[[science fiction|Science Fiction]]|location=Redwood City|publisher=Electronic Arts|year=2008|system=PC|scene=Virmire|isbn=9780784546642|oclc=246633669|text=Shepard: What do you want from us? Slaves? Resources?<br>My kind '''transcends''' your very understanding. We are each a nation. Independent, free of all weakness. You cannot grasp the nature of our existence.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[surpass]], as in [[intensity]] or [[power]]; to [[excel]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=c. 1698|author=w:John Dryden|title=Epitaph on the Monument of a Fair Maiden Lady
|passage=How much her worth '''transcended''' all her kind.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To [[climb]]; to [[mount]].
#: {{ux|en|lights in the heavens '''transcending''' the region of the clouds}}
#* {{RQ:Howell Epistolae|September 5 1632|To Sir Tho. Haw.|passage=your Muse soars up to the upper, and '''transcending''' that too, takes her fight among the Celestial bodies}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|to pass beyond the limits of something}} {{l|en|exceed}}, {{l|en|overgo}}, {{l|en|surpass}}; see also [[Thesaurus:transcend]]
* {{sense|to surpass something}} {{l|en|better}}, {{l|en|dwarf}}, {{l|en|eclipse}}; see also [[Thesaurus:exceed]]
* {{sense|to climb}} {{l|en|ascend}}

